![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

When loading optional files (such as the checkpoint or authorization config), any parsing or syntax errors should not be silently ignored. Currently, if `required` is `false`, any error (including `SyntaxError` from `JSON.parse`) is caught and silently returns `null` without recording diagnostics. To ensure the harness fails closed on malformed files, we should check if the error is a missing file (`ENOENT`). If the file exists but fails to load or parse, we must record a diagnostic and fail closed.

```suggestion
function safeReadJson(root, relPath, role, diagnostics, { required = true } = {}) {
  try {
    return readJson(root, relPath);
  } catch (error) {
    const isMissing = error instanceof Error && error.code === 'ENOENT';
    if (required || !isMissing) {
      diagnostics.push({
        code: 'input_file_load_failed',
        role,
        path: relPath,
        reason: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),
        severity: required ? 'critical' : 'warning',
      });
    }
    return null;
  }
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When loading parsed files (such as JSON), validate the parsed file shape, record malformed entry diagnostics, skip bad entries, and pass those diagnostics into the package validator to ensure it fails closed.
</details>

