![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The checkpoint input shape is not validated before accessing its properties. If the checkpoint is present but malformed (e.g., `completed_question_keys` or `output_rows` are not arrays), it could cause runtime TypeErrors. When validating expected array fields in input data, if a field is present but is not an array, we should record a validation failure (blocker) and process it as an empty array to ensure the system fails closed.

```javascript
  const existingCheckpoint = loadedInputs.checkpoint ?? null;
  if (existingCheckpoint) {
    if (typeof existingCheckpoint !== 'object' || Array.isArray(existingCheckpoint)) {
      diagnostics.push({
        code: 'input_shape_failure',
        reason: 'checkpoint is not a valid object',
        severity: 'critical',
      });
    } else {
      if (existingCheckpoint.completed_question_keys && !Array.isArray(existingCheckpoint.completed_question_keys)) {
        diagnostics.push({
          code: 'input_shape_failure',
          reason: 'checkpoint completed_question_keys is not an array',
          severity: 'critical',
        });
        existingCheckpoint.completed_question_keys = [];
      }
      if (existingCheckpoint.output_rows && !Array.isArray(existingCheckpoint.output_rows)) {
        diagnostics.push({
          code: 'input_shape_failure',
          reason: 'checkpoint output_rows is not an array',
          severity: 'critical',
        });
        existingCheckpoint.output_rows = [];
      }
    }
  }
  const skippedFromCheckpointCount = checkpointCompletedKeys(existingCheckpoint).length;
```

